<title>FRANCE: French October trade surplus 16.94 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French October trade surplus 16.94 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a record seasonally adjusted trade surplus in October of 16.94 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in September of 9.70 billion, provisional customs office data showed.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in September of 10.09 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					  October  September</p>
<p> Trade balance			16.94    9.70</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)     17.29    8.20</p>
<p> Imports			     113.14  115.60</p>
<p> Exports			     130.08  125.30</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	     5.75    4.95</p>
<p> Energy balance		     -7.69   -6.22</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance    14.84    6.78</p>
<p> Airbus exports	 3.64 (eight planes) 2.33 (six)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		     0.77    1.10</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports		142.31  124.06</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports		125.02  115.86</p>
<p> European Union			6.18    4.44</p>
<p> Germany				 0.73    0.04</p>
<p> Japan				  -1.42   -1.69</p>
<p> United States			-1.11   -2.57</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the first ten months of the year were as follows</p>
<p>				     Jan-Oct 1996     Jan-Oct 1995</p>
<p> Before seasonal adjustment   101.62		78.04</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	    103.02		79.20</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 54 52</p>
</text>
